    ]
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Shipping executive Paul Markland has travelled extensively in classic cars. For the Inca Trail rally with his son, he bought a Buick convertible and had it stripped and rebuilt, including stronger rear shock absorbers. He later published a diary of a London-to-Sydney journey made in company with eleven other classic cars.\n\nMarkland also served as secretary and a director of the Indochina Starfish Foundation, alongside his wife Myra’s earlier board involvement. The charity combines education and football programmes for disadvantaged Cambodian children, including accelerated learning to help those who have missed school catch up with their peers.",
    "html": "<p>Shipping executive Paul Markland has travelled extensively in classic cars. For the Inca Trail rally with his son, he bought a Buick convertible and had it stripped and rebuilt, including stronger rear shock absorbers. He later published a diary of a London-to-Sydney journey made in company with eleven other classic cars.</p>\r\n<p>Markland also served as secretary and a director of the Indochina Starfish Foundation, alongside his wife Myra’s earlier board involvement. The charity combines education and football programmes for disadvantaged Cambodian children, including accelerated learning to help those who have missed school catch up with their peers.</p>\r\n",
